287:\begin{lemma}[Albanese property over an algebraically closed field]
288:  \label{lem:pic0_isAlbanese_algClosed}
289:  \lean{AlgebraicGeometry.isAlbanese_pic0_of_isAlgClosed}
290:  \uses{def:IsAlbanese, thm:albanese_universal_property_northstar}
291:  Let \(C\) be a smooth proper geometrically integral curve over an
292:  algebraically closed field \(\bar k\), with representable Picard functor and
293:  genus \(g(C) > 0\), and let \(P \in C(\bar k)\) satisfy
294:  \(P \circ \iota_P = \eta\) for the Abel--Jacobi morphism \(\iota_P\) of
295:  \((C, P)\). Then \(\Pic^0_{C/\bar k}\) satisfies the Albanese universal
296:  property for the pointed curve \((C, P)\).
297:\end{lemma}
298:
299:\begin{proof}\leanok
300:  \uses{thm:albanese_universal_property_northstar}
301:  The universal property of \cref{def:IsAlbanese} has two clauses. The basepoint
302:  clause is the hypothesis. The factorisation clause --- every pointed morphism
303:  \(\varphi : C \to A\) into an abelian variety factors uniquely through
304:  \(\iota_P\) --- is \cref{thm:albanese_universal_property_northstar} at the same
305:  object, the Albanese development's Jacobian scheme being \(\Pic^0_{C/\bar k}\).
306:\end{proof}
